Make two webpages with the same underlying functionality. 

## First webpage

In the dotMotionSDTexperiment folder
Make a webpage that displays a random-dot kinematogram with sliders for coherence.

Buttons and sliders are at the bottom.

Sliders are:
- Number of dots (range: 100-600)
- Coherence (%) (range: 0->30)
- Radius of dots (pix)
- Speed of dots (pix/sec) (range: 10-300)
- Lifetime of dots (milliseconds) (range:30->500)

Pressing a reset button refreshes the dot pattern and randomly chooses whether the dot pattern will have zero coherence or the coherence specified by the slider.

A button at the bottom, "reveal answer", adds text indicating whether it is zero coherence or instead prints the coherence set by the slider.

